                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "The art style is interesting, and I genuinely wanted to play this game, but the controls are AWFUL, both on PC and mobile.\n\nI made it as far as the 3rd level, up to the piano section, where I eventually had to give up. What should probably be a simple sequence becomes incredibly frustrating because of how poorly the game handles movement and interaction.\n\nThe puzzles aren't much better. They often look straightforward, but the intended solutions can be quite different from what you'd naturally expect. It makes them feel more unintuitive than clever.\n\nWhat's even more frustrating is the lack of controller support. I feel like that would make the experience considerably more enjoyable.\n\nIt's a shame because I actually want to see the rest of the game. The visuals are appealing and there's clearly something interesting here, but the controls make progressing far more difficult than it should be.\n\n2/10 — I'd happily finish it if the controls didn't make me want to smash the keyboard over my head.",
